This extension adds NINJA GAIDEN: Master Collection modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Single extension supports all 3 games: NGS1, NGS2, NG3RE. Mod Loader will be installed automatically.[/summary]

Mod Loader  will be installed automatically.
This extension supports all 3 games in the collection with a single extension:
[list]
[*]NINJA GAIDEN Sigma (NGS1)
[*]NINJA GAIDEN Sigma 2 (NGS2)
[*]NINJA GAIDEN 3 Razor's Edge (NG3RE)
[/list]
Supports the Steam and Xbox versions of all 3 games. Other versions will need to specify the game folder manually when activating the game.
This extension will automatically download and install  [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/ninjagaidenmastercollection/mods/34]TMX Mod Loader[/url].

[color=#ea9999][size=3][b]You MUST run the Mod Loader using the included tool in the Vortex Dashboard tab [i][u]AFTER LAUNCHING THE GAME[/u][/i]. [/b][/size][/color]You may get a hex check error popup that you can safely ignore.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Tmx_NgLoader (Mods Loader) mods with a "tmx_ngloader.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Essential Files for NGS1 installs to the game folder, recognised by a "ninja gaiden sigma.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Essential Files for NGS2 is recognised by a "ninja gaiden sigma2.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Essential Files for NG3RE is recognised by a "ninja gaiden 3 razor's edge.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Mod Loader mods with a ".dat" file install to the "mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Databin Folder mods with a "databin" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Databin Subfolder mods with a "bgm" or "movie" folder install to the "databin" folder.[/*]
[*]Databin Subfolder mods are recognised by a "sound" or "movie" folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatically installs[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/818] [/url]Mod Loader.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for NINJA GAIDEN: Master Collection mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Xboxmodloader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "tmx_ngloader.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Ninjagaidensigma Steammodloader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "ninja gaiden sigma.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Ninjagaidensigma2 Steammodloader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "ninja gaiden sigma2.exe" file.

========================================================================

Ninjagaiden3razorsedge Steammodloader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "ninja gaiden 3 razor's edge.exe" file.

========================================================================

Mlmod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".dat" file.

  Installs to: "mods"

========================================================================

Databinfolder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "databin" folder.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Databinsubfolder1:

Recognised when the archive contains a "bgm" or "movie" folder.

  Installs to: "databin"

========================================================================

Databinsubfolder23:

Recognised when the archive contains a "sound" or "movie" folder.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine.
[/spoiler]

